[{"id":85666,"sender_id":854,"sender_full_name":"HDB","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4af4bcfbdb795ddeac40b881b07d5678?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Appearance.20of.20formulas/near/85666\">#1</a> Hello, I find the nLab a really nice wiki for math but there is one thing that bothers me: the appearance of math text. Sometimes parts of formulas like exponents are just way off where they normally sit and then it really looks quite ugly and deplaced. Is it just on my browser or what is the reason for that? In case this is universal, why don‘t we use some method to make formulas have nicer appearance?</p>\n<p>To not let you think wrongly of me, I want to assure that I think that the content is superb and I only try to understand what is the reason for me cringing at the display of text occasionally.</p>","timestamp":1600815471,"subject":"Appearance of formulas","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":85667,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Appearance.20of.20formulas/near/85667\">#2</a> I suspect it may be your browser or something else local.  Can you post a screenshot?</p>","timestamp":1600832121,"subject":"Appearance of formulas","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":85668,"sender_id":854,"sender_full_name":"HDB","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4af4bcfbdb795ddeac40b881b07d5678?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Appearance.20of.20formulas/near/85668\">#3</a> For example this line coming from <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/generalized%20%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29%20cohomology\">generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology</a>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>  </mtext><mspace></mspace><mspace width=\"0.1111em\"/><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.17em\"></mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">:</mo><mspace width=\"0.3333em\"/><mtext>  </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo><mover><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><mi>f</mi></mover></mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo><mover><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mover></mo><msup><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\tilde E \n    \\;\\colon\\; \n  (X \\stackrel{f}{\\longrightarrow} Y)\n    \\mapsto\n  (\\tilde E^\\bullet(Y) \n    \\stackrel{f^\\ast}{\\longrightarrow}\n  \\tilde E^\\bullet(X))\n  \\,.\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.5942em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6023em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">~</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1111em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.3333em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3442em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">⟶</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7581em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.011em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">↦</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.6424em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6023em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">~</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3924em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">⟶</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7581em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7633em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.011em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1702em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6023em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">~</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>The tildes and bullets float over the E‘s with a gap of half the size of the letter below. I‘m now on the safari browser, but the appearance of the site seems to be the same on the iPad version of Firefox, which should be the browser recommended on the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/HomePage\">HomePage</a> under Software requirements or am I missing something?</p>\n<p>Unfortunately I didn‘t manage to upload a screenshot but it will probably suffice if you just tell me wether you see this gap, too. Many thanks for your time in advance!</p>\n<p>Edit: Ok now I see that it works in this comment, there is no gap anymore, but I am quite surprised as it does still have a gap when clicking on the links, also on Firefox. Yet I did not provide an example even for myself. My question reduces to wether the copied and original line from the Cohomology entry are both displayed both in the exactly same way on your system. (Last remark: Strangely the nicer typesetting only appeared after publishing the comment, not in preview, don‘t know why.)</p>","timestamp":1600860365,"subject":"Appearance of formulas","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":85669,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Appearance.20of.20formulas/near/85669\">#4</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the nicer typesetting only appeared after publishing the comment, not in preview</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That piece of info might serve to nail down the problem, when Richard sees this.</p>","timestamp":1600865396,"subject":"Appearance of formulas","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]